      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T01:55:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Other than the strided_load functions below (which are rarely used, and hopefully on the chopping block), the skvx functions always return a new value instead of modifying the input, so this structure is a little surprising to me.\n\nOn the other hand, it\u0027s very handy to be able to pass back the computed length too.\nWhat do you think about having them be:\n\n    SIN std::pair\u003cVec\u003cN, double\u003e, double\u003e normalize(const Vec\u003cN, double\u003e\u0026 v) {\n        double len \u003d length(v);\n        return {v / len, len};\n    }\n    \nI suppose we could run into issues if std::pair\u003c\u003e doesn\u0027t play nice with over-aligned types, but the compilers will let us know.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 887,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 887,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "10cdad04487b6381050ccf27afa94f739ca67880",
